A||N||3||86SEFIERO||how much power will the 4cyl 5 speed take?||||1||
Z||000000||86SEFIERO||10-16-2000||01:15 AM||||<BR>I.m planning on doing a v-8 swap into a fiero and been wondering what you guys would go with for a 400 h.p small block?<BR>I also have the 4:10trans and the economy 4 speed both out of 84 fieros?<BR>Thankyou!!!! ||||reg||1
Z||000001||JetroGT||10-16-2000||06:24 AM||||Ask Archie. He does do the V8 swap with trans normally mounted to the L4 motor but 400 H.P. might be better suited to a 5spd Getrag or an auto.||||reg||3
Z||000002||mrfiero||10-16-2000||04:56 PM||||The Isuzu 5-sp. will probably work, but more than likely it will rip itself apart in no time (depends on how you drive it!).<P>The 4.10 tranny is a waste of time with a V-8......you will have to shift it so fast you'll get tired of it in no time (you could probably keep it in 4th gear all the time!)<P>The gears in the econo 4-sp. are spaced well enough to suit a V-8 and might ultimately be the best choice.  <P>The Getrag will hold up to it as well, but quite frankly 400HP is way too much for any of these trannies in the long run.<P>Good luck.....sounds like a nice Fiero!  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||10-16-2000||06:34 PM||||The 4.10 on a V8 will be a 3 speed. You'll almost never need or want 1st gear.<P>None of GM's transverse FWD transmissions is built for that much power. Just how long it will take to break one depends on how you run it and what if any work was done to prep it for the application.||||reg||1
